input.findings:
## Root cause

`Parallel#_updateAxesFromSeries` calls `axisHelper.niceScaleExtent()` **inside** the `ecModel.eachSeries` loop, i.e. once per (series x dimension), instead of once per axis after all series extents have been unioned. Because `niceScaleExtent` -> `getScaleExtent` -> `ensureScaleRawExtentInfo` **caches** a `ScaleRawExtentInfo` on the scale instance and then writes the result back with `scale.setExtent(...)`, the first series' data extent is frozen into the cache and every later series' contribution is thrown away.

Trace:

1. `src/coord/parallel/Parallel.ts:187` — `axis.scale.unionExtentFromData(data, data.mapDimension(dim))` grows `scale._extent` correctly (`src/scale/Scale.ts:120-134`, `_innerUnionExtent`).
2. `src/coord/parallel/Parallel.ts:188` — `axisHelper.niceScaleExtent(axis.scale, axis.model)`.
3. `src/coord/axisHelper.ts:68` — `const rawExtentResult = ensureScaleRawExtentInfo(scale, model, scale.getExtent()).calculate();`
4. `src/coord/scaleRawExtentInfo.ts:295-313` — `ensureScaleRawExtentInfo` returns the cached instance and **ignores the `originalExtent` argument** on every call after the first:
   ```ts
   let rawExtentInfo = scale.rawExtentInfo;
   if (rawExtentInfo) {
       return rawExtentInfo;
   }
   ```
   `_dataMin`/`_dataMax` are only set in `_prepareParams` (constructor, `src/coord/scaleRawExtentInfo.ts:92-96`).
5. `src/coord/axisHelper.ts:175` — `scale.setExtent(extent[0], extent[1]);` writes the **stale** min/max (from series #1) back onto the scale, clobbering the union performed at step 1.

So with two parallel series where series #2 has larger values on a dimension, e.g. series A `dim0` in [0, 10] and series B `dim0` in [0, 100]:
- after A: `_extent = [0, 10]`, rawExtentInfo cached with `_dataMin=0/_dataMax=10`, niced to `[0, 10]`
- after B: `unionExtentFromData` sets `_extent = [0, 100]`, but `niceScaleExtent` immediately resets it to `[0, 10]`.
Result: series B's lines are drawn far outside the axis / clipped, and axis labels stop at the first series' max. (Reverse series order and it "works", which is the classic symptom.)

Every other coordinate system already unions first and nices once, which is why they are not affected:
- `src/coord/cartesian/Grid.ts:511-553` (`_updateScale`: reset -> union all series) then `Grid.ts:120-174` (`updateAxisTicks` -> `niceScaleExtent` once per axis).
- `src/coord/polar/polarCreator.ts:80-101` (reset `setExtent(Infinity, -Infinity)`, union all series, then `niceScaleExtent` once per axis).

## The edit — `src/coord/parallel/Parallel.ts`

EXACT current code, `src/coord/parallel/Parallel.ts:173-191`:

```ts
    /**
     * Update properties from series
     */
    private _updateAxesFromSeries(parallelModel: ParallelModel, ecModel: GlobalModel): void {
        ecModel.eachSeries(function (seriesModel) {

            if (!parallelModel.contains(seriesModel, ecModel)) {
                return;
            }

            const data = seriesModel.getData();

            each(this.dimensions, function (dim) {
                const axis = this._axesMap.get(dim);
                axis.scale.unionExtentFromData(data, data.mapDimension(dim));
                axisHelper.niceScaleExtent(axis.scale, axis.model);
            }, this);
        }, this);
    }
```

EXACT replacement (full method body; the only semantic changes are the extent reset and hoisting `niceScaleExtent` out of `eachSeries`):

```ts
    /**
     * Update properties from series
     */
    private _updateAxesFromSeries(parallelModel: ParallelModel, ecModel: GlobalModel): void {
        // Reset scale extent before union, in case that `update` is performed
        // more than once on the same axes.
        each(this.dimensions, function (dim) {
            this._axesMap.get(dim).scale.setExtent(Infinity, -Infinity);
        }, this);

        ecModel.eachSeries(function (seriesModel) {

            if (!parallelModel.contains(seriesModel, ecModel)) {
                return;
            }

            const data = seriesModel.getData();

            each(this.dimensions, function (dim) {
                const axis = this._axesMap.get(dim);
                axis.scale.unionExtentFromData(data, data.mapDimension(dim));
            }, this);
        }, this);

        // `niceScaleExtent` must be called only after the extents of all of the series
        // have been unioned. Otherwise `scale.rawExtentInfo` (created and cached by
        // `ensureScaleRawExtentInfo` in the first `niceScaleExtent` call) keeps the data
        // extent of the first series, and the subsequent `niceScaleExtent` calls reset
        // the scale extent back to that stale value, discarding the data extent of the
        // rest of the series.
        each(this.dimensions, function (dim) {
            const axis = this._axesMap.get(dim);
            axisHelper.niceScaleExtent(axis.scale, axis.model);
        }, this);
    }
```

Notes on the replacement:
- `each` is the file-local alias `const each = zrUtil.each;` (`src/coord/parallel/Parallel.ts:44`), and `axisHelper` is already imported (`src/coord/parallel/Parallel.ts:29`). No new imports needed.
- The `each(this.dimensions, function (dim) {...}, this)` + `this._axesMap.get(dim)` pattern is already used in the same file (`_init`, lines 122-145, and line 185-189), so `this`-typing compiles as-is. If you prefer, `this._axesMap.each(axis => ...)` also works (`HashMap#each` exists at `node_modules/zrender/src/core/util.ts:748`), but the dimension-driven loop keeps deterministic axis order.
- The reset loop is defensive only: today `Parallel` (and therefore its scales) is recreated on every `coordSysMgr.create` (`src/coord/parallel/parallelCreator.ts:37`, called at `src/core/echarts.ts:1811` right before `coordSysMgr.update` at `src/core/echarts.ts:1824`), so extents start at `[Infinity, -Infinity]`. It mirrors `Grid._updateScale` / `updatePolarScale`. It can be dropped if you want the minimal diff — the load-bearing change is hoisting `niceScaleExtent`.

## Files that do NOT need changes (verified)

- `src/coord/parallel/ParallelAxis.ts` — no extent logic; `setExtent` on the axis is the *pixel* extent, set in `_layoutAxes` (`Parallel.ts` ~line 275+). Unaffected.
- `src/coord/parallel/parallelCreator.ts` — only creates/resizes; `update` is invoked by `CoordinateSystemManager.update` (`src/core/CoordinateSystem.ts:84-86`). Unaffected.
- `src/coord/axisHelper.ts`, `src/coord/scaleRawExtentInfo.ts`, `src/scale/Scale.ts` — the caching in `ensureScaleRawExtentInfo` is intentional (dataZoom and `defaultAxisExtentFromData` rely on the single cached instance per scale, see `src/component/dataZoom/AxisProxy.ts:405-412` `setDeterminedMinMax` + `freeze`, and `src/coord/cartesian/defaultAxisExtentFromData.ts:128-135, 243-249` `modifyDataMinMax`). Do NOT "fix" it by invalidating the cache — that would change cartesian/dataZoom behaviour. Fix the caller (parallel) instead.
- `src/coord/parallel/AxisModel.ts`, `ParallelModel.ts` — no change.

